{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThree `.github` files contain repeated or stale comments identified by the audit and revalidated on current `origin/main`. The pull-request template is user-facing documentation and is not subject to ticket-style terseness; only its redundant hidden routing comment is in scope.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only standalone configuration comments and the hidden HTML routing comment. Preserve YAML data and all visible contributor guidance byte-for-byte.\n\n## Scope\n- `codeql/codeql-config.yml` — Preserve that `docs/**` is excluded as non-shipping prose/experiments and that the default query suite is unchanged. Consumers: CodeQL workflow, packaging policy, maintainers.\n- `dependabot.yml` — Correct the stale Actions-only heading while preserving advisory-PR posture under Gerrit, weekly GitHub Actions and uv ecosystems, deliberate cooldown omission, and the MCP major-version ignore/removal condition. Consumers: Dependabot and repository-lock policy. Stale user-facing consumer docs are tracked by `rhyolite-saddening-aidi`.\n- `pull_request_template.md` — Condense at most the hidden Gerrit-routing reminder. Preserve all visible instructions and links unchanged. Consumers: GitHub contributors and docs-link checks.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only standalone comments or blank lines in the three declared files; visible user-facing text remains exact.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer contract has a PASS row with concrete before/after citations in a leaf-linked session log authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited comment block has an independent `bloat-removal` PASS row confirming that redundant, obvious, duplicated, historical, or stale prose was removed while current non-obvious rationale remained.\n- [ ] Documentation index checks, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and repository lint pass; no missing or FAIL semantic-preservation row remains.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded comment-only guard, documentation-index check, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788602427826637001,"uuid":"d415d208-564a-469f-9950-d46ff9aae3f1"}